Legacy computer architecture partitions a single physical wave-evolution process into artificial ontologies—instruction fetch/decode, register renaming, cache-coherency directories, OS thread schedulers, SRAM routing tables, and TCP/IP packet headers—each burning silicon area, energy, and tail latency reconciling boundaries that do not exist in the underlying mathematics.

In `lib/hx-lux.hypercubical` (`43rd` engine: `hx lux`), every computation and communication event across all five physical machine scales reduces to two scale-free primitives:
1. **`LuxChord` (Zero-Table Geodesic Deflection):** Legacy headers retract idempotently onto the intrinsic syndrome delta $\Delta s = s_{\text{src}} \oplus s_{\text{dst}}$ (`lux-thm-strip-retract`, `lux-thm-strip-idem`). Routing executes in **0 bytes of SRAM** via cyclic polynomial shift-XOR ($g_{23}(x) = x^{11}+x^9+x^7+x^6+x^5+x+1 = \texttt{0xAE3}$ on the $N = 2{,}048$ Golay-23 diamond orb, `lux-thm-golay23-perfect-2048 = refl`) paired with a single De Morgan antipodal reflection chord cutting hypercube diameter strictly in half across all dimensions (`hd-thm-folded-diam-half`).
2. **`LuxPlaquette` (1-Cycle Cryptic Boundary Interaction):** A 4-edge elementary 2-cell $(e_N, e_E, e_S, e_W) \in (\mathbb{F}_2^{64})^4$ satisfies exact discrete Maxwell/Stokes coboundary closure $(v_0 \oplus v_1) \oplus (v_1 \oplus v_2) \oplus (v_2 \oplus v_3) \oplus (v_3 \oplus v_0) \equiv 0$ (`lux-thm-stokes-plaquette-zero`) while evaluating 64 parallel conjugated Lafont cuts in **1 hardware cycle** (`lop3.b32` on Hopper `sm_90a`, single LUT4/LUT6 on ASIC/FPGA).
